id: pm-brand-rendered-accessibility
title: Locate failing accessibility pairs in consumer components
description: "Accept local components' resolved brand-token roles and diagnose consumer foreground/background/focus compositions, retaining theme and token references. Add typed SDK and CLI, typed remedies, strict bounded input, docs and packed non-git acceptance."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: accessibility,cli,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-27T18:50:52.962Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T19:14:01.506Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Fixtures distinguish text, focus and decorative rules; every failing pair has a component locator and measured ratio; JSON/TOON reports fit a requested budget without hiding failure counts."
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T18:51:15.372Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: src/contrast.ts contrastAudit certifies 68 fixed kit pairs (36 text, 4 focus, 28 decorative), not consumer compositions. pm-web owns application/browser accessibility; core SDK owns universal output shaping and accounting. Sibling and core source searches plus GitHub search found no equivalent consumer fault locator. Scope is a pure read-only diagnostic: no tracker import/export/sync, plans, claims, leases, status inference or mutations; tracker invariants remain applicable to validation evidence only. Registry reports pm CLI 2026.10.27; keep the repository SDK pin at 2026.10.23."
  "2026-10-27T18:51:21.176Z",codex-agent,"Design: explicit resolved colors plus brand-token references, theme and component locator; text (4.5 or explicit large-text 3), focus (3), decorative (no failure threshold). Reuse existing WCAG contrast primitives. Keep complete fault records; an insufficient budget returns a typed refusal with full failure counts rather than shortened locators. Lazily load the public SDK through standard package imports for core shaping/accounting, allow host injection, and keep pure diagnostics independent of the optional SDK peer. Validate with seeded adversarial serialization/replay sequences, non-git SDK read-back and packed npm/Bun install modes."
  "2026-10-27T19:07:25.574Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and focused verification pass: 7/7 tests; 500 seeded sequences and 6000 operations with older-input replays, CRLF/whitespace variants, native parent/dependency fields and SDK read-back after each sequence. New-source coverage is 100/100/100/100 at unchanged thresholds. Six independent behavioral reverts fail in disposable copies (measurement, classification, locator, threshold, dense arrays, budget). Public-tracker evidence: 14 certified items, 84 comparisons, baseline 0 failures; controlled overrides yield 56 failures (28 text, 28 focus), 28 decorative exemptions. At budget 512 JSON/TOON refusals use 65/63 estimated tokens and retain all counts; complete reports use 3043/1152. Native state and copied-file hashes remain unchanged; see docs/accessibility-validation.md. Local strict health with inherited extensions reports pm-github host-version skew; do not change the SDK pin or global extension. Use no-extensions locally and clean CI for full gates. The report SDK is now a required peer so all CLI acquisition modes can install it automatically; pure diagnosis still never loads the host."
  "2026-10-27T19:10:45.851Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm test --run --progress --shared-host-safe passed all 4 linked commands: typecheck, lint, focused 7/7 tests and 6/6 disposable revert proofs. Project test-result tracking is disabled, so this comment records the observed run rather than enabling tracking. No-extensions strict health passes with zero warnings. Packed project-local npm/Bun and npm-global JSON/TOON cases pass; isolated Bun-global setup is being corrected before remaining runner acceptance. Added arbitrary IEEE-754 input/output fuzzing and own-property boundary isolation; no persistent state is introduced."
  "2026-10-27T19:13:58.039Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance completed: all 6 acquisition modes (npm local, Bun local, npm global including the real pm host symlink, Bun global, npx, bunx) passed both JSON and TOON, 12/12 CLI scenarios, plus both public-export/native-render consumer smokes. Every mode consumed the same captured tarball and its SHA-256 remained unchanged. The final full npm/Bun release gates run in CI; do not run saturated-host full suites. Scope review: no SDK capability gaps found, no tracker mutation/import/sync or status-role decision paths, no shared mutable persistent state. Refusals are bounded and retain all completed failure counts. Limits: callers supply resolved component roles; this is not a DOM/browser conformance audit."
